;
; How Pannier files a parcel in MUMPS as MYRA (pannier_rules.h PR6): each
; freight of a parcel under its peer (one digit) and the parcel's number
; (9 digits), the freight's place in the parcel (6 digits); the node holds
; the parcel's bytes (8 digits, 16 MiB at most), the attempts made (2),
; its tracking status (1, caravan_rules.h CR5) and when it last changed,
; in seconds since 1970 (12). The rules say what the values may mean;
; this says whether they make a record.
^ZXPANNIER(peer:i1, parcel:i9, freight:i6) = size:i8! ^ attempt:i2! ^ state:i1! ^ stamp:i12!
